<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Item

A row that shows content with media and actions, such as a list entry, a notification, or a setting. Compose it from `Item`, `ItemMedia`, `ItemContent`, `ItemTitle`, `ItemDescription`, and `ItemActions`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Item, ItemContent, ItemTitle, ItemDescription, ItemActions } from "#lib/components/ui/item/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<Item variant="outline">
	<ItemContent>
		<ItemTitle>Basic item</ItemTitle>
		<ItemDescription>A simple item with a title and a description.</ItemDescription>
	</ItemContent>
	<ItemActions>
		<Button variant="outline" size="sm">Action</Button>
	</ItemActions>
</Item>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/item.json
```

## Anatomy

`ItemMedia` sits at the start and holds an icon, avatar, or image. `ItemContent` takes the room in the middle, with an `ItemTitle` and an `ItemDescription` clamped to two lines. `ItemActions` sits at the end. `ItemHeader` and `ItemFooter` take a full row above or below the content, since the item wraps.

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default`, `outline`, or `muted`. Set `variant` on `ItemMedia` to `icon` for an icon in a bordered square, or `image` to crop an image to a square.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Item variant="muted">
	<ItemMedia variant="icon"><ShieldAlertIcon /></ItemMedia>
	<ItemContent>...</ItemContent>
</Item>
```

## Link

Set `href` to render the whole item as a link. Link items fill on hover and show a focus ring.

<Demo section="link" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Item variant="outline" href="/docs/components">
	<ItemContent>
		<ItemTitle>Visit the components</ItemTitle>
	</ItemContent>
	<ItemActions><ChevronRightIcon /></ItemActions>
</Item>
```

## Group

Wrap items in `ItemGroup` to make a list; the group renders `role="list"` and each item `role="listitem"`. Place `ItemSeparator` between items to divide them.

<Demo section="group" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ItemGroup>
	{#each people as person, index (person.email)}
		{#if index > 0}<ItemSeparator />{/if}
		<Item>...</Item>
	{/each}
</ItemGroup>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, like the shadcn item, and the padding, gap, text size, and corner radius follow the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Item variant="outline" size="sm">...</Item>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius that follows `size`.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Item variant="outline" rounded="3xl">...</Item>
```

## API

`Item` extends the native `div` attributes, or the `a` attributes when `href` is set. `ItemDescription` extends the `p` attributes, and every other part extends the `div` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface ItemBaseProps {
	/** `default` is transparent; `outline` draws a border; `muted` fills the background */
	variant?: "default" | "outline" | "muted";
	/** Padding, gap, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

type Props = ItemBaseProps & ((CompPropsWithChild<"div"> & { href?: undefined }) | (CompPropsWithChild<"a"> & { href: string }));

interface MediaProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** `default` shows the media as is; `icon` puts an icon in a bordered square; `image` crops an image to a square */
	variant?: "default" | "icon" | "image";
}
```
